OL,3,GNEWSANo bathing warning after water in
OL,4,Abrook turns blue
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople have been urged to avoid bathing
OL,7,Fin a brook after its water turned blue.
OL,9,FThe Environment Agency (EA) said it was
OL,10,Finvestigating a pollution incident at
OL,11,FLittleham Brook in Exmouth, Devon.
OL,13,FIt said it suspected the pollution was
OL,14,Ffrom an industrial source and had
OL,15,Fclassed it as a category one incident -
OL,16,Fthe most serious - due to the "severe
OL,17,Fenvironmental impact and the
OL,18,Fsignificant time the brook will need to
OL,19,Frecover".
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
